From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:08:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] fix: never emit CullDistance as a stage-out member

Problem: shaders writing a standalone CullDistance output fail to compile
in Metal (out.gl_CullDistance has no such member).

Root cause: Metal has no cull-distance output; CullDistance only exists
as a local array copied to [[user(cullN)]] varyings, but builtin_to_glsl
still qualified it with the stage-out struct.

Fix: name CullDistance outputs as the local array. Primitives are not
culled by it (Metal has no equivalent).

Verified by: compile errors gone in the vkd3d-proton test sweep,
59 -> 12 failures in the affected tests (see NOTES.md Finding 12).

Off switch: none.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index 1f8a913..3bf914f 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -19137,6 +19137,10 @@ string CompilerMSL::builtin_to_glsl(BuiltIn builtin, StorageClass storage)
 	case BuiltInClipDistance:
 	case BuiltInCullDistance:
 	case BuiltInLayer:
+		// Metal has no cull-distance output; CullDistance only exists as a local array (copied to
+		// [[user(cullN)]] varyings), never as a member of the stage-out struct.
+		if (builtin == BuiltInCullDistance && storage == StorageClassOutput)
+			break;
 		if (is_tesc_shader())
 			break;
 		if (is_mesh_shader())
